        "output_index": 1,
        "sequence_number": 82,
        "text": "This pixel appears to be **white** (or a very light color). \n\nThat said, I should note that with a single 1×1 pixel on a white background, it can be hard to tell whether the pixel itself is truly white or whether it's just blending in with the background around it. If you have access to the file, you could check its exact RGB values with an image editor or a color picker tool — for example, pure white would be RGB (255, 255, 255).",
